cannot be more than ten feet by six.  A small cot is bolted to the
floor, and the floor slopes toward an uncovered drainage hole in the
middle of the room, streaked with rust where the iron bolts have
corroded.  Manacles hang from the back wall, and in them are two
skeletal hands, all that remains of what once must have been a human
being.  The way out lies north.
